# End-to-End XGBoost 2.1.4 Large-Scale Training & Inference Plan (Strict Float32)

## 1. Hardware & Resource Budget
* **Source Storage:** Google Cloud Storage (GCS) — ~400GB+ compressed Parquet (`float32` schema)
* **Compute:** 16-Core CPU, 64GB System RAM
* **Local Cache Disk:** 200GB NVMe/SSD mount (strictly for compressed quantized bin pages)
* **Accelerator:** 1x NVIDIA L4 GPU (24GB VRAM)

| Resource | Physical Limit | Safe Working Target | Pipeline Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **GCS Bucket** | Unlimited | Raw `f32` Parquet Shards | Source of truth & prediction sink (zero local raw files) |
| **System RAM** | 64 GB | **< 45 GB** | Holds 1 unpacked `f32` batch (~1.5GB) + quantile sketches |
| **Local Disk** | 200 GB | **< 150 GB** | Stores quantized `uint8` bin pages (~4x compression from `f32`) |
| **L4 GPU VRAM** | 24 GB | **< 18 GB** | Receives quantized pages on-the-fly for histogram splits |

